  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader in any topic list, I want to swipe a row from right to left to add or remove the favourite, and use a second swipe option to add or remove the super favourite, so that I can manage my flags from every list and not only from the flag views. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-13.)\n\n### Observed\n\nThe current trailing swipe action \"Supprimer\" exists only in the views that list flags (Favoris, Suivis, Lus). In \"Tous\" and in the category topic lists, a row offers no flag action.\n\n### Expected\n\n- **Swipe from right to left, first action:** \"Ajouter aux favoris\" when the topic is not a favourite, \"Retirer des favoris\" when it is.\n- **Second action:** \"Ajouter aux super favoris\" or \"Retirer des super favoris\", by the same rule.\n- Available in **every** topic list (categories, Tous, Favoris, Suivis, Lus, search results), with the label following the topic's current state.\n- The writes go through the existing flows: the favourite write `TopicFlagFlow` (LOT-051, confirmed-session rule of #314) and the super-favourites store (`SuperFavoritesStore`). No new HFR request without a capture.\n\n### To check before coding\n\n- Legacy at `87fe0d1c`: the swipe sets of each list, for parity and to cite in the PR.\n- Overlap with **LOT-177 (#417, M5: uniform swipe set in every list)**. This request is narrower, flag actions only. Decide whether it is M4 (operator feedback) or folded into #417. Proposal: **M4 for these two actions**, and #417 keeps the rest.\n- Same row component as group L (#817, #825, #647, #648): fix it in the shared row, under the grouped-claim rule (#836).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Both actions exist in every topic list, and the label follows the current state (add or remove).\n- [ ] The favourite write is confirmed by HFR's own answer, as #314 requires. A failure is shown, and the row keeps its old state.\n- [ ] Model tests cover the four transitions; each test is shown to fail without the change.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
